<Folder><name>1 · Bases &amp; hotels</name><open>0</open>
<Placemark>
<name>D1 · HSM Hotel San Martino — Garbagnate Monastero</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 1 — Mon 5 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #hotel #d1-d4 #freeparking #d1<br><br>Nights 5-8 Oct. 24h reception, free parking, no restaurant. ~500 m off the SS36 — ask for a room away from the road.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=HSM+Hotel+San+Martino+Garbagnate+Monastero">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_base</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>9.301,45.772,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D1 · Milan Malpensa T1 — arrive &amp; depart</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 1 — Mon 5 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #airport #start #end #d1<br><br>Land 19:00 D1. Depart ~23:00 D15. Eat landside here on arrival night. Be at the rental return lot by 20:00 on D15 — confirm the return terminal matches your flight terminal.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Milano+Malpensa+Terminal+1">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_base</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>8.7281,45.6306,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D5 · The Oswald Grand Hotel — Selva di Val Gardena</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 5 — Fri 9 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #hotel #d4-d8 #confirm #d5<br><br>Nights 8-12 Oct. PIN IS APPROXIMATE — confirm the exact address, and ask about the Selva restricted-traffic zone and plate registration.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=The+Oswald+Grand+Hotel+Selva+di+Val+Gardena">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_base</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>11.759,46.556,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D8 · B&amp;B Hotel Passo Tre Croci — Cortina</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 8 — Mon 12 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #hotel #d8-d12 #1805m #d8<br><br>Nights 12-16 Oct, at 1,805 m. The Lago di Sorapis trailhead is at the door. Hard frost most nights. Ask them about trail 215 ice conditions.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=B%26B+Hotel+Passo+Tre+Croci+Cortina">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_base</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>12.19,46.573,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D12 · Venice — stay in Dorsoduro or Cannaregio</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 12 — Fri 16 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #hotel #d12 #tobook #d12<br><br>Night 16 Oct. NOT YET BOOKED. Dorsoduro for romance (Zattere at sunset), Cannaregio for easy logistics. Stay on the island, not Mestre.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Dorsoduro+Venezia">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_base</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>12.327,45.431,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D13 · Lake Garda — south-west shore</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 13 — Sat 17 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #hotel #d13-d14 #tobook #d13<br><br>Nights 17-19 Oct. NOT YET BOOKED. Salo / Desenzano / Sirmione / Padenghe — all ~2h to MXP. Shortlist: Bellerive (Salo), Acquaviva (Desenzano), Villa Arcadio (Salo hills).<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Sirmione+Lago+di+Garda">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_base</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>10.607,45.493,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>2 · Main plan — sights &amp; hikes</name><open>0</open>
<Placemark>
<name>D2 · Bellagio — ferry pier &amp; old town</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 2 — Tue 6 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #sight #town #ferry #d2<br><br>D2 afternoon. Arrive as a foot passenger from Cadenabbia. Villa Melzi gardens EUR10, open to 19:00. Golden hour 17:45-18:55.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Bellagio+imbarcadero">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_main</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>9.2617,45.9857,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D2 · Sunset boat — Bellagio / Varenna</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 2 — Tue 6 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #boat #splurge #romantic #d2<br><br>D2. Private hour ~EUR150-200, or shared from ~EUR40pp. October light on this lake is the best of the year. Book ahead — October fleets are reduced.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Bellagio+boat+tour">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_main</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>9.26,45.986,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D2 · Villa Carlotta — Tremezzo</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 2 — Tue 6 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #sight #villa #rainproof #d2<br><br>D2. Open daily, 10:00-19:00 to 18 Oct. ~EUR15-17.50. Real art inside (Canova, Hayez) — the one villa that survives a wet day.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Villa+Carlotta+Tremezzo">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_main</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>9.2231,45.9853,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D2 · Villa del Balbianello — Lenno</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 2 — Tue 6 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #sight #villa #booknow #closedWed #d2<br><br>D2. Gardens ~EUR13-14, + 45-min interior tour ~EUR24-25. CLOSED Mon AND Wed — this is why the west shore goes on Tuesday. Book the interior tour ahead.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Villa+del+Balbianello+Lenno">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_main</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>9.2103,45.9694,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D3 · Orrido di Bellano — gorge walkway</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 3 — Wed 7 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #sight #gorge #EUR8 #betterinrain #d3<br><br>D3, end of the walk. EUR8 adult. Lit walkway bolted into a gorge. Better with more water in it, but CAN CLOSE on high water — check before driving over.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Orrido+di+Bellano">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_main</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>9.301,46.0424,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D3 · Sentiero del Viandante — Varenna start (Olivedo)</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 3 — Wed 7 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #hike #3h #530m #slipperywet #d3<br><br>D3. ~3h, ~530 m ascent to Bellano. Up Via della Croce from Olivedo, via Vezio and Regolo. POLISHED LIMESTONE — genuinely slippery wet; don&#x27;t do it in a downpour.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Olivedo+Varenna">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_main</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>9.2847,46.0119,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D3 · Villa Monastero — Varenna</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 3 — Wed 7 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #sight #villa #closedTue #rainproof #d3<br><br>D3. Garden + house museum EUR15, garden only EUR13. Last entry 17:30. CLOSED TUESDAYS — hence Varenna on Wednesday. Furnished period rooms = indoor option.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Villa+Monastero+Varenna">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_main</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>9.286,46.0075,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D4 · Bergamo Citta Alta — Piazza Vecchia</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 4 — Thu 8 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #sight #town #lunch #ztl #d4<br><br>D4 lunch stop, directly on the A4. Funicular up ~EUR3 return, every 5-10 min. Eat casoncelli alla bergamasca. NEVER drive up — hard ZTL plus Lombardy emissions rules.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Piazza+Vecchia+Bergamo">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_main</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>9.6626,45.7038,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D5 · Col Raiser gondola — Santa Cristina (CHEAPER ROUTE)</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 5 — Fri 9 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #lift #cheaper #quieter #preferred #d5<br><br>D5 preferred start. Runs to 1 Nov, materially cheaper than the EUR74 Ortisei cable car, far quieter. From the top walk up via Pieralongia (~+400 m, 1h15-1h30) — this is the bit the closed Fermeda chairlift used to do.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Col+Raiser+Santa+Cristina+Val+Gardena">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_main</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>11.72,46.565,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D5 · Ortisei–Furnes–Seceda cable car (CLASSIC ROUTE)</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 5 — Fri 9 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #lift #EUR74 #to2Nov #d5<br><br>D5 alternative. ~EUR74 return, first up 08:30. Fastest way to the famous view. Park at the station — Ortisei centre is one of the longest pedestrian zones in the Dolomites.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Ortisei+Seceda+cable+car">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_main</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>11.6743,46.5793,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D5 · Rifugio Firenze / Regensburgerhutte</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 5 — Fri 9 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #hut #lunch #closes12Oct #d5<br><br>D5 lunch. CLOSES 12 OCTOBER — one of your last chances. Service 11:30-15:00. Reachable ~25 min on path 4 from the top of Col Raiser.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Rifugio+Firenze+Regensburger+Hutte">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_main</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>11.7043,46.5928,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D5 · Seceda — the ridge</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 5 — Fri 9 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #hike #view #weatherdependent #d5 #d5<br><br>D5. THE most weather-dependent day of the trip — in cloud you pay for fog. Ridge walk 8.9 km, +575 m, 3-3.5h. Move it to any clear day in the block.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Seceda">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_main</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>11.6503,46.6081,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D6 · Adolf Munkel Weg — Zannes/Zans trailhead</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 6 — Sat 10 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #hike #9km #378m #parkingbooking #d6<br><br>D6 morning. 9.2 km circuit, +378 m, 3-3.5h, easy-moderate, along the base of the Odle north wall. ZANNES CAR PARK MAY NEED AN ONLINE BOOKING IN 2026 — check before driving up.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Zannes+Val+di+Funes">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_main</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>11.707,46.6355,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D6 · Chiesa di Santa Maddalena — Val di Funes</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 6 — Sat 10 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #sight #photo #walkonly #d6<br><br>D6. The most photographed building in South Tyrol. NON-RESIDENT CARS ARE BARRED from the panorama viewpoint May-Nov — park in the village and walk 20-30 min.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Santa+Maddalena+Val+di+Funes">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_main</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>11.6997,46.642,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D6 · Torggelen — Villandro / Villanders</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 6 — Sat 10 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #food #highlight #booknow #rainproof #d6<br><br>D6 afternoon, 15 min from Zannes. Certified farms: Oberpartegger, Winklerhof, Pschnickerhof — linked by walking trails. PHONE AHEAD: season nominally starts early Oct but many farms open mid-month. Indoors = rain-proof.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Villandro+Villanders+Alto+Adige">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_main</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>11.54,46.63,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D7 · Alpe di Siusi / Compatsch</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 7 — Sun 11 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #hike #meadow #easy #45h #d7<br><br>D7 afternoon. Up to 14.4 km, +483 m, 4.5h, easy. Europe&#x27;s largest high meadow. Best in low afternoon light. Open huts: Sassopiatto (to 18 Oct), Alpe di Tires (to 19 Oct), Schgaguler (to 1 Nov).<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Compatsch+Alpe+di+Siusi">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_main</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>11.62,46.54,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D7 · Forcella Sassolungo &#x27;coffin&#x27; gondola — Passo Sella</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 7 — Sun 11 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #lift #closes11Oct #datecritical #d7<br><br>D7, 09:30. CLOSES 11 OCTOBER — you cross this pass on the 12th, one day too late. Two-person standing cabins that never stop; 5 min up to Rifugio Toni Demetz at 2,681 m. Date is single-sourced — VERIFY EARLY. Wind can hold it even in clear weather.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Forcella+Sassolungo+cable+car+Passo+Sella">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_main</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>11.7595,46.5093,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D7 · Mont Seuc gondola — Ortisei (use this one on D7)</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 7 — Sun 11 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #lift #to2Nov #dontdriveup #d7<br><br>D7. Runs to 2 Nov, and it&#x27;s the side you arrive from after Passo Sella. DON&#x27;T DRIVE UP to Compatsch — road closed to non-residents 09:00-17:00 and parking needs an online reservation.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Ortisei+Alpe+di+Siusi+cable+car">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_main</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>11.676,46.574,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D8 · Canazei — Val di Fassa</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 8 — Mon 12 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #town #coffee #lunch #d8<br><br>D8, ~11:00. Main town of the Ladin Val di Fassa, at the hub of the four great passes. Coffee and lunch stop. Sass Pordoi cable car almost certainly closed by now.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Canazei+Val+di+Fassa">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_main</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>11.769,46.477,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D8 · Lago di Carezza / Karersee</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 8 — Mon 12 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #lake #photo #goearly #20min #d8<br><br>D8, ~09:30. Emerald lake reflecting the Latemar. Paid car park on the SS241 with an underpass to the shore; boardwalk loop 20-30 min. GO EARLY — you need still water, and the coaches arrive late morning. No swimming, no going to the water&#x27;s edge.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Lago+di+Carezza+Karersee">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_main</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>11.576,46.409,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D9 · Cadini di Misurina viewpoint</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 9 — Tue 13 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #hike #easy #exposed #dryonly #d9<br><br>D9, add-on. 3.9 km, +144 m, 1-1.5h on trail 117 from Rifugio Auronzo. THE FINAL SPUR IS A NARROW, EXPOSED PATH ON A ROCK NOSE — dry conditions only, skip it if there&#x27;s frost or fresh snow.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Cadini+di+Misurina+viewpoint">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_main</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>12.29,46.605,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D9 · Lago di Braies / Pragser Wildsee</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 9 — Tue 13 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #lake #before9am #noreservation #d9<br><br>D9, arrive ~08:00. Sunrise 07:26 — leave the hotel at 07:00. Still water, empty boathouse, coaches still an hour out. Shore loop 3.5 km flat, ~1h. NO RESERVATION NEEDED IN OCTOBER (that system runs 1 Jul-15 Sep). Survives mist well.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Lago+di+Braies+Pragser+Wildsee">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_main</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>12.085,46.695,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D9 · Rifugio Locatelli — CLOSED, no food or shelter</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 9 — Tue 13 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #closed #warning #d9<br><br>D9. CLOSED for the season. It sits at the far side of the Tre Cime loop, so there is no food, water or shelter for the middle two-thirds. Wind at Forcella Lavaredo is brutal in October — carry everything.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Rifugio+Locatelli+Dreizinnenhutte">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_main</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>12.308,46.625,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D9 · Tre Cime di Lavaredo — Rifugio Auronzo</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 9 — Tue 13 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #hike #EUR40 #prebook #best #d9<br><br>D9. BOOK THE SLOT at pass.auronzo.info — EUR40/car, plate required, 12h validity, autumn access ~08:00-18:00. Loop 8.8-10 km, +425 m, 3-4h anticlockwise. ~700 spaces at the rifugio.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Rifugio+Auronzo+Tre+Cime+di+Lavaredo">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_main</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>12.296,46.613,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D10 · Lago Federa / Croda da Lago</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 10 — Wed 14 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #hike #larches #hutlunch #rainok #d10<br><br>D10. THE most famous larch location in the Dolomites, 2,046 m. Rifugio Croda da Lago / Palmieri is the most reliable hut lunch of the Cortina leg — call +39 0436 862085. Overcast light is GOOD for larches.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Lago+Federa+Rifugio+Croda+da+Lago">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_main</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>12.0787,46.5006,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D10 · Ponte de Ru Curto — Lago Federa trailhead</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 10 — Wed 14 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #trailhead #freeparking #d10<br><br>D10 start. Free trailhead parking. 8.4 km / +469 m / 3h out-and-back, or the 13.1 km / +700 m / 5h circuit.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Ponte+de+Ru+Curto+Cortina">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_main</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>12.102,46.516,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D11 · Cinque Torri — WWI open-air museum</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 11 — Thu 15 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #hike #wwi #chairliftclosed #carryfood #d11<br><br>D11. Restored trenches and tunnels among the five towers. CHAIRLIFT CLOSES 11 OCT and all three huts (Scoiattoli, Nuvolau, Cinque Torri) are shut — walk up from Col Gallina and carry food.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Cinque+Torri+Cortina">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_main</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>12.045,46.515,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D11 · Col Gallina — free parking, Cinque Torri trailhead</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 11 — Thu 15 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #trailhead #freeparking #d11<br><br>D11. Free parking on the SR48 opposite Ristorante da Strobel. Circuit 9.6 km, +600 m, ~3h45 via Lago di Limedes to Rif. Averau, Nuvolau and Cinque Torri. Nuvolau&#x27;s final ridge is narrow with a cable.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Col+Gallina+Passo+Falzarego">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_main</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>12.025,46.523,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D11 · Lagazuoi cable car — Passo Falzarego</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 11 — Thu 15 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #lift #lastoneopen #to18Oct #d11<br><br>D11. THE ONLY LIFT STILL RUNNING in Cortina — to 18 Oct. Free parking at the pass. First up 09:00, every 15 min, LAST DOWN 17:00. Terrace lunch at 2,752 m — call +39 0436 867303.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Passo+Falzarego+Lagazuoi+cable+car">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_main</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>12.0086,46.5192,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D12 · Rialto market</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 12 — Fri 16 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #market #saturday #morning #d12<br><br>D13, 09:00. Saturday morning is the good one — fish, produce, noise. All&#x27;Arco is a minute away.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Mercato+di+Rialto+Venezia">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_main</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>12.335,45.44,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D12 · Tronchetto parking — Venice</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 12 — Fri 16 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #parking #EUR29 #maxheight210 #d12<br><br>D12, arrive ~14:00. EUR29 per 24h, covered, 3,483 spaces. MAX HEIGHT 2.10 m — check your car isn&#x27;t a tall SUV. Easiest arrival: you never leave the causeway. People Mover to Piazzale Roma ~EUR1.50.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Venezia+Tronchetto+Parking">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_main</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>12.301,45.443,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D14 · Castello Scaligero — Sirmione</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 14 — Sun 18 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #sight #castle #d14<br><br>D14. Water-moated Scaliger castle guarding the entrance to the old town. Sirmione at night, once the day-trippers have gone, is the good version.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Castello+Scaligero+Sirmione">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_main</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>10.607,45.493,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D14 · Grotte di Catullo — Sirmione</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 14 — Sun 18 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #sight #roman #rainbreaks #d14<br><br>D14, 09:30. Vast Roman villa ruin in an olive grove at the tip of the peninsula, water on three sides. Go early, before the coaches. OPEN RUIN — the one thing on D14 that rain ruins.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Grotte+di+Catullo+Sirmione">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_main</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>10.607,45.505,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
</Folder>
