</Folder>
<Folder><name>5 · Rain &amp; cold fallbacks</name><open>0</open>
<Placemark>
<name>D2 · Como Duomo + Museo della Seta — wet-day swap</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 2 — Tue 6 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #rain #indoor #d2 #d2<br><br>D2 RAIN PLAN. The Duomo is free and one of the great Gothic/Renaissance hybrids in Italy. The silk museum is far better than it sounds — Como was the silk capital of Europe. Also Tempio Voltiano, Basilica di Sant&#x27;Abbondio. Skip the Brunate funicular: you&#x27;d pay to sit in a cloud.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Duomo+di+Como">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_rain</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>9.0832,45.8103,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D3 · Accademia Carrara, Bergamo — best wet day on the Como leg</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 3 — Wed 7 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #rain #indoor #swapWedThu #d3<br><br>D3 RAIN PLAN. Botticelli, Bellini, Raphael, Titian. SWAP WEDNESDAY AND THURSDAY and do Bergamo today — it costs nothing because Thursday&#x27;s Bergamo stop was optional anyway. Plus arcaded Citta Alta, Santa Maria Maggiore, Cappella Colleoni.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Accademia+Carrara+Bergamo">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_rain</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>9.673,45.705,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D3 · Lecco museums — Villa Manzoni &amp; Palazzo delle Paure</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 3 — Wed 7 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #rain #indoor #EUR6 #d3<br><br>D3 local rain option. EUR6 each. Villa Manzoni is the family home of the man who wrote Italy&#x27;s national novel about THIS shore. Lecco&#x27;s Wednesday market (Piazza Garibaldi, 07:30-14:00) is thin in heavy rain.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Villa+Manzoni+Lecco">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_rain</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>9.3878,45.8497,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D5 · Otzi — South Tyrol Museum of Archaeology, Bolzano</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 5 — Fri 9 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #rain #indoor #bestwetday #d5<br><br>THE best wet-weather destination of the whole trip, ~50 min down the valley from Selva. The 5,300-year-old iceman found in a glacier up the road. Use it for whichever Val Gardena day is a write-off. Bolzano also has the arcaded Portici and the Duomo.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Museo+Archeologico+Alto+Adige+Bolzano+Otzi">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_rain</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>11.351,46.4991,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D5 · Vallunga — flat, low, forested, fine in drizzle</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 5 — Fri 9 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #rain #easyhike #25h #d5<br><br>Val Gardena drizzle option, straight from Selva. Flat gravel track up a glacier-carved valley under the Puez walls, 2.5h return, larches everywhere. Pay-and-display at Parcheggio Vallunga. Also the D8 slow-morning fallback.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Vallunga+Selva+di+Val+Gardena">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_rain</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>11.781,46.559,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D7 · Terme Merano — the cold/wet Sunday answer</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 7 — Sun 11 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #rain #spa #thermal #romantic #d7<br><br>D7 RAIN PLAN, ~1h15 from Selva. Large thermal complex, indoor AND outdoor pools, big sauna world. Being outside in hot water in cold rain is not a consolation prize. Merano has covered arcades and the Kurhaus too.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Terme+Merano+Therme+Meran">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_rain</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>11.1607,46.6688,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D8 · Brunico / Bruneck — Messner Mountain Museum Ripa</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 8 — Mon 12 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #rain #indoor #checkhours #d8<br><br>D8 RAIN PLAN, on the valley fallback route. Handsome market town; the castle holds MMM Ripa, on the mountain peoples of the world. CHECK OCTOBER HOURS.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Messner+Mountain+Museum+Ripa+Brunico">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_rain</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>11.937,46.796,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D9 · Dobbiaco / Toblach — Mahler &amp; cultural centre</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 9 — Tue 13 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #rain #indoor #d9<br><br>D9 rain option, on the way back from Braies. Gustav Mahler composed here; the Grand Hotel is now a cultural centre.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Dobbiaco+Toblach">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_rain</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>12.222,46.735,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D9 · San Candido / Innichen — church + Acquafun pool</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 9 — Tue 13 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #rain #indoor #pool #checkhours #d9<br><br>D9 RAIN PLAN — bail north instead of east. Beautiful Romanesque collegiate church, and Acquafun indoor pool/wellness centre. CHECK HOURS. Save the EUR40 and book Tre Cime for another day — this is exactly why you don&#x27;t book it early.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=San+Candido+Innichen+Acquafun">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_rain</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>12.279,46.733,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D10 · Cortina museums — Zardini fossils &amp; Rimoldi art</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 10 — Wed 14 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #rain #indoor #checkhours #d10<br><br>D10 RAIN PLAN. Museo Paleontologico Rinaldo Zardini (these mountains are a fossilised coral reef — a good thing to learn while looking at them) and the Mario Rimoldi modern art collection, both in the Ciasa de ra Regoles. Small municipal museums — CHECK OCTOBER HOURS.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Musei+delle+Regole+Cortina+d%27Ampezzo">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_rain</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>12.137,46.539,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D11 · Forte Tre Sassi — WWI museum, Passo Valparola</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 11 — Thu 15 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #rain #indoor #ontheme #checkhours #d11<br><br>D11 RAIN PLAN. A restored Austro-Hungarian fort covering exactly the WWI front you&#x27;d have been walking at Cinque Torri and Lagazuoi — with a roof. Seasonal: CHECK OCTOBER HOURS.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Forte+Tre+Sassi+Passo+Valparola">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_rain</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>11.993,46.529,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D12 · Gallerie dell&#x27;Accademia — Venice</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 12 — Fri 16 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #rain #indoor #dorsoduro #d12<br><br>D12 rain plan, minutes from a Dorsoduro hotel. Venice is genuinely rain-proof; the October risk is ACQUA ALTA, not rain. Check the city tide forecast the night before and buy rubber overshoes.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Gallerie+dell%27Accademia+Venezia">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_rain</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>12.328,45.4314,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D12 · Peggy Guggenheim Collection</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 12 — Fri 16 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #rain #indoor #dorsoduro #d12<br><br>D12 rain plan. Modern art on the Grand Canal, a few minutes from the Accademia.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Peggy+Guggenheim+Collection+Venezia">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_rain</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>12.3316,45.4308,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D12 · Scuola Grande di San Rocco — Tintoretto</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 12 — Fri 16 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #rain #indoor #underrated #d12<br><br>D12 rain plan. Tintoretto&#x27;s entire cycle, in the room he painted it for. One of the great interiors in Europe and never crowded.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Scuola+Grande+di+San+Rocco+Venezia">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_rain</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>12.326,45.4368,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D14 · Aquaria Thermal SPA — Sirmione</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 14 — Sun 18 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #rain #spa #thermal #d14<br><br>D14 RAIN PLAN, and the best one on the trip. Sulphurous thermal spring, indoor and outdoor pools, five minutes from the castle. Everything else on D14 already has a roof: the winery, the olive oil museum, the Valeggio lunch.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Aquaria+Thermal+SPA+Sirmione">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_rain</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>10.608,45.494,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D14 · Museo dell&#x27;Olio d&#x27;Oliva — Cisano</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 14 — Sun 18 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #rain #indoor #free #d14<br><br>D14. Free museum and shop, open daily. Mid-October is the start of the Garda DOP olive harvest.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Museo+dell%27Olio+di+Oliva+Cisano+Bardolino">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_rain</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>10.73,45.53,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D14 · Verona — Arena, Castelvecchio, Duomo</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 14 — Sun 18 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #rain #indoor #ztl #d14<br><br>D14 rain option, 30 min from Sirmione. Mind the ZTL: Mon-Fri 10:00-13:30 and 16:00-18:00, Sat-Sun 10:00-13:30. Park at Cittadella.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Arena+di+Verona">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_rain</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>10.994,45.439,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>6 · Optional &amp; swaps</name><open>0</open>
<Placemark>
<name>D3 · Lecco Wednesday market — Piazza Garibaldi</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 3 — Wed 7 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #optional #market #wedonly #d3<br><br>D3 alternative, 07:30-14:00, 50+ stalls. Runs 4 Mar - 25 Nov 2026. Wednesday 7 October falls perfectly in your stay.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Piazza+Garibaldi+Lecco">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_opt</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>9.393,45.856,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D5 · Cristauta / Praplan — fully-on-foot Seceda start</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 5 — Fri 9 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #optional #bighike #900m #d5<br><br>D5 hardcore option. Trail 4 up to the ridge — but with FERMEDA CLOSED it&#x27;s a +900-1,000 m climb with no shortcut. Real, but a big first day in the mountains.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Santa+Cristina+Val+Gardena">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_opt</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>11.728,46.562,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D6 · Geisler Alm / Rifugio delle Odle</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 6 — Sat 10 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #optional #hut #maybeclosed #d6<br><br>D6. You flagged this as a &#x27;no go&#x27; — I&#x27;d push back gently. It&#x27;s directly ON the Adolf Munkel Weg, so you pass its door regardless. The busy/commercial complaint is a high-summer problem. THE REAL RISK IS THAT IT&#x27;S SHUT — October season unverified.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Geisler+Alm+Rifugio+delle+Odle+Villnoss">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_opt</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>11.7,46.63,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D8 · Segra Sacun market — Ortisei, 12 Oct only</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 8 — Mon 12 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #optional #fallback #d8 #d8<br><br>D8 FALLBACK, 08:00-16:00. The biggest traditional market of the year — food stalls, crafts, and a tradition of men giving women a decorated pear. CLASHES with the 08:00 Great Dolomites Road start; you can&#x27;t have both. Take it if you want a slow morning or it rains.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Ortisei+Sankt+Ulrich+centro">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_opt</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>11.672,46.576,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D9 · Lago di Misurina — 10-minute stop</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 9 — Tue 13 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #optional #photo #ontheway #d9<br><br>D9. Directly on the Tre Cime road and you pass it twice — take whichever light is better. The Grand Hotel Misurina reflected with the Sorapis group behind. Col de Varda chairlift closed 20 Sep.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Lago+di+Misurina">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_opt</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>12.253,46.583,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D10 · Lago di Sorapis — FLEX day, from the hotel door</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 10 — Wed 14 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #flex #hike #ICERISK #microspikes #d10<br><br>FLEX. Trailhead is at Passo Tre Croci. 11.5 km out-and-back, ~500 m, ~4h. TRAIL 215 HAS CABLED EXPOSED LEDGES, METAL LADDERS AND POLISHED ROCK, all north/east-facing and shaded — ICED LADDERS ARE A REAL OCTOBER RISK. Rif. Vandelli closed 20 Sep: no water, shelter or toilet. Mildest driest day only, mid-morning start, CARRY MICROSPIKES, turn back if there&#x27;s ice. Ask the hotel the night before.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Lago+di+Sorapis+Passo+Tre+Croci">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_opt</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>12.2264,46.5726,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D11 · Monte Mondeval from Passo Giau — full-day option</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 11 — Thu 15 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #optional #hike #5h #d11<br><br>D11 alternative. 12.8 km, ~5h, moderate, open and panoramic, larch-rich. A full-day substitute for the Lagazuoi/Cinque Torri pair.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Passo+Giau">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_opt</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>12.054,46.479,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D11 · Val Travenanzes descent from Lagazuoi</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 11 — Thu 15 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #optional #hike #carshuttle #d11<br><br>D11 alternative. Cable car up, walk down a wild hanging valley to Ponte Outo on the SR48 — 4-5h, mostly descent, some cabled steps near the forcella. NEEDS A CAR SHUTTLE.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Val+Travenanzes+Cortina">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_opt</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>12.0,46.53,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>7 · Passes &amp; drive stops</name><open>0</open>
<Placemark>
<name>D8 · Passo Campolongo / Arabba — short route</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 8 — Mon 12 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #pass #shortroute #d8<br><br>On the short pass route (Gardena - Corvara - Campolongo - Arabba - Falzarego, 85 km, 2h45), the fallback if you skip Carezza and Canazei.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Arabba+Livinallongo">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_pass</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>11.872,46.497,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D8 · Passo Falzarego — 2,105 m</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 8 — Mon 12 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #pass #2105m #lagazuoi #d8<br><br>D8 and D11. Free parking, and the base of the Lagazuoi cable car — the only lift still running in Cortina. Kept open through winter, so October is never in doubt.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Passo+Falzarego">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_pass</styleUrl>
<Point><coordinates>12.009,46.519,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>D8 · Passo Gardena — 2,121 m (short route + sunset)</name>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Day 8 — Mon 12 Oct</b><br><b>Tags:</b> #pass #2121m #sunset #shortroute #d8<br><br>The short-route alternative for D8. Also the best zero-effort sunset of the Val Gardena leg — Sassolungo framed by golden larches, 15 min from Selva.<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Passo+Gardena">▶ Open exact location in Google Maps</a>]]></description>
<styleUrl>#s_pass</styleUrl>
